{
  "$comment": [
    "CONTRACT FIXTURE — the credit-card JV body, pinned across two implementations.",
    "",
    "The wizard builds its JV in the browser (frontend/src/lib/ccJv.ts +",
    "hooks/credit-card/useOcrSubmission.ts) because a human reviews it there. Email",
    "automation has no browser, so backend/app/services/cc_jv.py builds the same body.",
    "Both suites tested their own side; nothing tested that the two agreed, and drift",
    "there posts wrong money silently. This file is the single source both read.",
    "",
    "Readers:",
    "  backend/tests/unit/test_cc_jv.py::test_contract_fixture",
    "  frontend/src/lib/ccJv.contract.test.ts",
    "",
    "SHAPE NOTE — the two builders take mappings differently, which is why this file",
    "keeps them apart instead of pre-merging:",
    "  TS      buildJvRows(details, { mappings, paymentAmount: paymentTypes })",
    "  Python  build_jv_rows(details, { **mappings, **paymentTypes })",
    "",
    "DELIBERATE DIFFERENCES, asserted per-side rather than ignored:",
    "  UserModified  empty from the wizard, 'OCR-EMAIL' from email ingest. The field",
    "                exists precisely to tell a machine-posted JV from a reviewed one",
    "                (CARMEN_INTEGRATION.md section 4 point 3), so it is NOT in",
    "                `expected` — each test asserts its own side's value.",
    "  JvhDate       Python emits '+00:00', JS emits '.000Z' — same instant, different",
    "                string. Compare as instants, never as strings.",
    "  fuzzy match   canonical_payment_type()'s Thai-diacritic folding is backend-only:",
    "                the wizard has a human to fix a misread, email ingest does not.",
    "                Every payment-type key below matches exactly, so folding never",
    "                engages and the shared arithmetic is what gets compared.",
    "",
    "PADDING IS LOAD-BEARING. docDate must be zero-padded DD/MM/YYYY. Unpadded,",
    "new Date('2026-8-5') is parsed as LOCAL time by JS and lands on the previous day",
    "in UTC (verified: 2026-08-04T17:00:00Z at ICT), while Python datetime(2026,8,5)",
    "does not move. Both producers pad today — normalizeDateStringToCE() at extraction",
    "and formatDateToDDMMYYYY() in the date picker — so the divergence is unreachable.",
    "Keep it that way."
  ],

